so the question is who is  the next big star of the republican  party  well there was a phenomenal piece  written this week by a good good friend  of mine cliff schechter  writing for the daily beast the piece is  titled dan crenshaw is the trumpiest of  the wannabe new  trumps  and in the piece he talks about the fact  that sure we've got other conservatives  out there kind of you know hinting at  and testing the waters you got your  nikki haley's of course you got your ted  cruz maybe they're the ones to take up  the mantle of trumpism here in the u.s  and then of course you've got the really  wackier ones your marjorie taylor greens  and your boberts  and your gates's  but none of them cliff points out  have what dan crenshaw has  dan crenshaw  for the most part  is not as openly extreme as some of  those other individuals  he knows how to speak to an audience he  effectively has as cliff points out what  trump had  that charisma  coupled with of course shamelessness and  cruelty  but it's the charisma  it's his ability to play to an audience  much like donald trump did  that is what makes crenshaw so dangerous  and of course most likely the heir  apparent to donald trump's entire  political movement  you know crenshaw recently did an  interview where he called out the  performance artists  of the republican party  and he told us we know who they are he  didn't want to name any names he doesn't  want to make any waves because he's  smart i'll give him that he is smart  he's good at what he does  but it's pretty obvious that he is  talking about your marjorie taylor  greens and your lauren boberts the  people and madison cawthorns the people  who are out there just to get famous  they just want people to know their  names and as he pointed out correctly by  the way  they're not doing anything legislatively  okay they're not actually furthering the  conservative cause as he says  and his ability to call these people out  and seem  as he's calling them out like the  rational choice like the best  alternative  is what does make him so incredibly  dangerous as a potential candidate in  the future  and then of course  you have the performative side  crenshaw has something the rest of them  don't  he's got military credentials and as  cliff schechter points out again  he's got the battle wound  he's got the eye patch  and i'm not saying that to attack him  but that eye patch is a constant  reminder  that he served  that he went over there and fought the  fight  that these other conservatives only push  from behind their legislative desks  that makes a big  difference  with these republican candidates  somebody who can go out there and say oh  well you say you support the military  but i was actually in it i fought it  and i live with the ramifications of it  he's got that tough guy persona that  donald trump could only pretend to have  and of course you do have the  performance artist in him right  we've all seen the videos that crenshaws  point out uh put out excuse me himself  you know rappelling down from the  ceilings acting like some kind of  avenger slash secret agent guy this big  tough bravado  of only i can save this  which is kind of similar to what donald  trump actually said  when he first ran for president only i  can do this  and that's what crenshaw is putting out  there  he appeals to the trumpers  but he can act sane enough  because i do think to his credit i think  he is a sane person  but i think he knows when to turn on the  crazy and turn it off and that's what  separates him from the rest of the pack  that's what makes him different from a  marjorie taylor green  it's what makes him different from a ted  cruz because ted cruz has gone full  blown into all of this he doesn't know  who he is  but crenshaw  can turn it on and turn it off like that  and as cliff points out  that's something that makes him  incredibly valuable  to the conservative movement and of  course makes him incredibly scary  as a potential 